<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en-GB">
<head>
    <%- include('partials/google-tag') %>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Taxi Websites That Book Into Your Dispatch System | Arrington</title>
    <%# INDEXABLE (13/10/2026): in the sitemap, no noindex, not in the main
        navigation. The Taxi websites ad group lands here. Copy approved by
        Tom on 13/10/2026 (see routes/taxiWebsites.js for what it may and may
        not say). %>
    <meta name="description" content="A £999 taxi and private hire website where online bookings go straight into iCabbi, Autocab, Cordic or another system with a booking API.">
    <link rel="canonical" href="https://www.arringtonconsultancy.com/taxi-and-private-hire-operators/websites">
    <%- include('partials/page-schema', { schemaName: 'Taxi and private hire websites', schemaPath: '/taxi-and-private-hire-operators/websites', schemaParent: { name: 'Taxi and private hire operators', path: '/taxi-and-private-hire-operators' }, schemaService: 'Taxi and private hire websites with bookings into the dispatch system' }) %>
    <meta property="og:type" content="website">
    <meta property="og:title" content="Taxi websites that book into your dispatch system | Arrington Consultancy">
    <meta property="og:description" content="A £999 taxi and private hire website where online bookings go straight into your dispatch system.">
    <meta property="og:url" content="https://www.arringtonconsultancy.com/taxi-and-private-hire-operators/websites">
    <meta property="og:image" content="https://www.arringtonconsultancy.com/img/logo">
    <meta name="csrf-token" content="<%= csrfToken %>">
    <link rel="icon" href="/favicon.ico" sizes="any">
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
    <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=DM+Sans:ital,wght@0,400;0,500;0,700;1,400&family=Poppins:wght@500;600&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
    <style nonce="<%= nonce %>">
        :root {
            <% for (const [prop, val] of Object.entries(theme.vars)) { %>
            <%= prop %>: <%= val %>;
            <% } %>
        }
        * { box-sizing: border-box; }
        body { margin: 0; font-family: 'DM Sans', sans-serif; background: var(--black); color: var(--text); line-height: 1.6; }
        <%- include('partials/site-chrome-styles') %>

        h1, h2, h3 { font-family: 'Poppins', 'DM Sans', sans-serif; font-weight: 600; color: var(--text-bright); line-height: 1.2; margin: 0; }
        p { color: var(--text); margin: 0 0 1.2rem; }

        .btn { display: inline-block; font-family: 'DM Sans', sans-serif; font-size: 0.92rem; font-weight: 600; padding: 0.6rem 1.5rem; border-radius: 3px; text-decoration: none; cursor: pointer; border: 1px solid transparent; }
        .btn-primary { background: var(--accent); color: var(--black); border-color: var(--accent); }
        .btn-primary:hover, .btn-primary:focus-visible { background: var(--accent-hover); border-color: var(--accent-hover); }

        main { padding: 0 0 5rem; }
        .tw-wrap { max-width: 700px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 0 1.5rem; }

        /* HERO: the taxi page's treatment and the same real photo of Tom, so
           an operator arriving from the ad sees the same firm as the taxi
           page. No generated or stock images. */
        .tw-hero { position: relative; overflow: hidden; background: var(--black); display: flex; align-items: center; min-height: 640px; padding: calc(var(--site-chrome) + 3.5rem) 1.5rem 4rem; }
        .tw-hero-photo { position: absolute; top: var(--site-chrome); right: 0; bottom: 0; left: 0; margin: 0; }
        .tw-hero-photo img { display: block; width: 100%; height: 100%; object-fit: cover; object-position: 72% 12%; }
        .tw-hero-photo::after { content: ''; position: absolute; inset: 0; background: linear-gradient(90deg, var(--black) 0%, var(--black) 28%, color-mix(in srgb, var(--black) 60%, transparent) 52%, color-mix(in srgb, var(--black) 10%, transparent) 78%, transparent 100%), linear-gradient(0deg, var(--black) 0%, transparent 22%); }
        .tw-hero-inner { position: relative; z-index: 1; width: 100%; max-width: 1100px; margin: 0 auto; }
        .tw-hero-text { max-width: 600px; }

        .tw-label { font-size: 0.72rem; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.14em; font-weight: 700; color: var(--accent); margin-bottom: 1rem; display: block; }
        h1 { font-size: clamp(1.6rem, 4.6vw, 2.3rem); margin-bottom: 1.2rem; text-wrap: balance; }
        .tw-lede { font-size: 1.12rem; color: var(--text-bright); margin-bottom: 1.6rem; max-width: 62ch; }
        .tw-hero-demo { margin: 1rem 0 0; font-size: 0.97rem; }
        .tw-systems { margin: 1rem 0 0; font-size: 0.9rem; color: var(--text-muted); }

        .tw-section { margin-top: 3.25rem; }
        .tw-section > h2 { font-size: 1.4rem; margin-bottom: 0.9rem; }
        .tw-section > p { max-width: 62ch; }

        .tw-cred { margin-top: 3.25rem; padding: 1.5rem 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--border); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); }
        .tw-cred h2 { font-size: 1.4rem; margin-bottom: 0.9rem; }
        .tw-cred p { max-width: 62ch; }
        .tw-cred p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }
        .tw-indep { color: var(--text-bright); font-weight: 500; }

        .tw-link { color: var(--accent); text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 40%, transparent); padding-bottom: 2px; }
        .tw-link:hover, .tw-link:focus-visible { border-bottom-color: var(--accent); }

        /* WHAT THE £999 COVERS: scope, which is what the paper surface is
           reserved for. The price is read from the offer catalogue. */
        .tw-band { margin-top: 3.5rem; padding: 3.25rem 0 3.5rem; }
        .tw-band .tw-section { margin-top: 0; }
        .tw-price { font-family: 'Poppins', 'DM Sans', sans-serif; font-size: 2.2rem; font-weight: 600; color: var(--text-bright); margin: 0 0 0.6rem; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
        .tw-actions { margin: 1.6rem 0 0; }
        .tw-also { margin: 2.25rem 0 0; font-size: 0.97rem; }

        /* THE OFFICE WORKSPACE: a plain list of examples under the website's
           price band. */
        .tw-list-lead { margin-bottom: 0.6rem; color: var(--text-bright); font-weight: 500; }
        .tw-list { margin: 0 0 1.4rem; padding-left: 1.2rem; max-width: 62ch; }
        .tw-list li { margin-bottom: 0.7rem; color: var(--text); }
        .tw-list li::marker { color: var(--accent); }

        /* THE DEMO SCREENSHOT: two phone screens on the demo's own dark
           ground, linked to the live demo. */
        .tw-demo-shot { display: block; margin: 1.4rem 0 1rem; border-radius: 10px; overflow: hidden; border: 1px solid var(--border); }
        .tw-demo-shot img { display: block; width: 100%; height: auto; }
        .tw-demo-shot:hover, .tw-demo-shot:focus-visible { border-color: var(--accent); }
        .tw-demo-link { margin: 0; }

        @media (max-width: 760px) {
            .tw-hero { display: block; min-height: 0; padding: var(--site-chrome) 0 0; }
            .tw-hero-photo { display: block; position: relative; top: auto; height: 38vw; max-height: 240px; }
            .tw-hero-photo img { object-position: 66% 6%; }
            .tw-hero-photo::after { background: linear-gradient(0deg, var(--black) 0%, color-mix(in srgb, var(--black) 40%, transparent) 30%, transparent 60%); }
            .tw-hero-inner { padding: 0 1.5rem; margin-top: -1.5rem; }
            h1 { margin-bottom: 1rem; }
            .tw-lede { font-size: 1.02rem; margin-bottom: 1.25rem; }
            .tw-section { margin-top: 2.1rem; }
            .tw-cred { margin-top: 2.1rem; padding: 1.25rem 0; }
            .tw-band { margin-top: 2.5rem; padding: 2.5rem 0 2.75rem; }
            .tw-actions .btn, .tw-hero-actions .btn { width: 100%; text-align: center; }
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <%- include('partials/site-header', { currentPage: { slug: 'taxi-and-private-hire-operators' }, navPages, canEdit: false, content, pageContact }) %>

    <%# HERO. The reason to choose us over a web agency leads (bookings into
        dispatch). The email check was named here until Tom's decision of
        15/10/2026 took it out of the £999; since 17/10/2026 it is one of the
        office workspace's examples, at the foot of the page. %>
    <header class="tw-hero">
        <picture class="tw-hero-photo">
            <source srcset="/img/startup/tom-at-desk.webp" type="image/webp">
            <img src="/img/startup/tom-at-desk.jpg" alt="Tom Arrington at his desk" width="1672" height="941" fetchpriority="high">
        </picture>
        <div class="tw-hero-inner">
            <div class="tw-hero-text">
                <span class="tw-label">Taxi and private hire websites</span>
                <h1>A taxi website that sends bookings straight into your dispatch system</h1>
                <p class="tw-lede" data-hero-lede>We build websites for taxi and private hire operators where a booking made online lands in your dispatch system like any other job, so nobody in the office has to key it in. <%= '£' + (websiteOffer.pricePence / 100).toLocaleString('en-GB') %>, with the dispatch link included.</p>
                <div class="tw-hero-actions">
                    <a href="#conversation" class="btn btn-primary">Tell us about your firm</a>
                </div>
                <%# A text link, not a second button: the enquiry stays the one
                    call to action (Tom's approval, 15/10/2026). %>
                <p class="tw-hero-demo" data-hero-demo><a class="tw-link" href="<%= demoUrl %>">See a taxi site we built</a></p>
                <p class="tw-systems" data-systems>Works with iCabbi, Autocab, Cordic and other systems with a booking API.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </header>

    <main>
        <div class="tw-wrap">
        <%# Google Ads worker's brief of 13/10/2026, approved by Tom as written:
            a supporting point, so it is short and sits under the hero; the page
            still leads with dispatch. The scope stays as "What the £999 website
            covers" states it. %>
        <div class="tw-section" data-scratch>
            <h2>Built from scratch for your firm</h2>
            <p>No templates. We design the site around your firm, how your customers book and what you want it to say, and if we'd do something differently we'll tell you straight. If there's a site in the trade you rate, we'll take what works about it and build it in your name.</p>
        </div>

        <%# THE DEMO (taxi demo brief, 15/10/2026, section 8): operators buy on
            seeing one. Tidewell Cars is invented and its site says so on every
            page; the screenshot is that site, taken from a real test booking.
            The line "Book a test job and see it go through." is the brief's. %>
        <div class="tw-section" data-demo>
            <h2>See one we built</h2>
            <p>Tidewell Cars is an Exmouth taxi firm we invented to show what the <%= '£' + (websiteOffer.pricePence / 100).toLocaleString('en-GB') %> gets you. Book a test job and see it go through. The booking goes into a test dispatch system, the dispatch reference comes straight back, and a few seconds later you see the driver, the car and how far away it is. No car will come.</p>
            <a class="tw-demo-shot" href="<%= demoUrl %>">
                <picture>
                    <source srcset="/img/taxi-demo/tidewell-demo.webp" type="image/webp">
                    <img src="/img/taxi-demo/tidewell-demo.jpg" alt="The Tidewell Cars demo on a phone: the home page with its price form, and a confirmed booking showing the dispatch reference, the driver, the car and the arrival time" width="1100" height="885" loading="lazy">
                </picture>
            </a>
            <p class="tw-demo-link"><a class="tw-link" href="<%= demoUrl %>">Open the Tidewell Cars demo</a></p>
        </div>

        <div class="tw-section" data-dispatch>
            <h2>How the booking gets to dispatch</h2>
            <p>A taxi website has one job, which is getting the booking. Ours also get it into dispatch. The booking form on your website talks to your dispatch system through that system's booking API, so when a customer books, the job appears in dispatch ready for your controllers to allocate, the same as one taken on the phone.</p>
            <%# The qualifier the brief asked for: the link is promised only where
                access can be arranged. Vendor access is outside our control. %>
            <p data-qualifier>We connect to iCabbi, Autocab and Cordic, and to other systems with a booking API. The link is included in the £999 where your system has a booking API and you can arrange API access with your provider. Some providers approve the connection or issue a key first, and on the first call we'll tell you what yours will need. Any charge your provider makes for API access is between you and them.</p>
            <p data-widget>If your provider's own booking widget already does what you need, we'll say so.</p>
        </div>

        <%# Facts: nearly twenty years owning Abacus (Evidence case study); the
            last eight or so on iCabbi (Tom's approved email of 6 July 2026,
            APPROVED 03: "used iCabbi for around 8 years before selling the
            business"), checked before publishing as the approval required. %>
        <div class="tw-section" data-operator>
            <h2>Built by someone who ran taxi firms</h2>
            <p>Tom Arrington owned and ran Abacus and Falmouth Taxis for nearly twenty years, the last eight or so on iCabbi. A general web agency can build you a good looking site. What it usually can't do is get the booking into dispatch, because it has never sat on the other side of that screen. <a class="tw-link" href="/evidence#biography__2">Read the Abacus and Falmouth Taxis story</a>.</p>
        </div>

        <%# Keeps the live ad headline "We Do Not Sell Software" true. The last
            sentence is the taxi page's approved independence line, word for
            word. %>
        <div class="tw-cred" data-independence>
            <h2>Your dispatch system stays as it is</h2>
            <p>We build the website and leave your dispatch system exactly as it is. The website sits in front of the system you already run and hands it the booking.</p>
            <p class="tw-indep">We're listed on the iCabbi Marketplace, but we don't sell software and no supplier pays us.</p>
        </div>
        </div>

        <section class="tw-band surface-paper">
        <div class="tw-wrap">
        <div class="tw-section" data-covers>
            <h2>What the £999 website covers</h2>
            <p class="tw-price"><%= '£' + (websiteOffer.pricePence / 100).toLocaleString('en-GB') %></p>
            <p>That's the whole price. It starts with a recorded planning conversation to agree what the site needs to do. You then get a complete first version and one structured round of changes before launch. The link to your dispatch system is part of it, not an extra.</p>
            <div class="tw-actions">
                <a href="#conversation" class="btn btn-primary">Tell us about your firm</a>
            </div>
            <p class="tw-also" data-dispatch-advice>Choosing or changing a dispatch system as well? <a class="tw-link" href="/taxi-and-private-hire-operators">Talk to an operator first</a>.</p>
        </div>
        </div>
        </section>

        <%# THE OFFICE WORKSPACE (17/10/2026). Google Ads brief "Taxi page: the
            £999 office workspace", this worker's proposal, approved by Tom as
            written ("yes"), with "made up" unhyphenated for the page's no dash
            rule. After the website's price on purpose, so no reader takes the
            workspace's £999 as part of the website's. The only place on this
            page that says "AI" (Brand OS: AI workers as part of the offer, never
            the hook). Compliance is keeping track and warning, and the operator
            signs off; the email check is described as the 13/10 approval
            describes it. No payment button: the enquiry form below is the
            action. %>
        <div class="tw-wrap">
        <div class="tw-section" data-workspace>
            <h2>An office workspace for your firm</h2>
            <p>Alongside the website, we can set up an office workspace: AI workers built for your firm, who know your business, your customers and how you talk to them. They draft the work and flag what needs attention, and someone in your office checks it and decides what goes out.</p>
            <p class="tw-list-lead">What they can take off the office:</p>
            <ul class="tw-list">
                <li>Keeping track of every driver badge, vehicle licence, DBS check, insurance and MOT date, and warning you before anything runs out. You still check the paperwork and sign off anything that goes to the council.</li>
                <li>Checking the bookings that still come by email. Account customers, hotels and schools still book that way, so each request is matched against the jobs in your dispatch system, and a booking that was never keyed in, or was keyed in wrong, gets flagged before the customer is left waiting.</li>
                <li>Drafting quotes from your own prices.</li>
                <li>Helping plan driver rotas and cover.</li>
                <li>Writing social media posts in your firm's voice, ready for you to approve.</li>
            </ul>
            <p data-workspace-price>The workspace is <%= '£' + (workspacePricePence / 100).toLocaleString('en-GB') %>, separate from the website, or <%= '£' + ((websiteOffer.pricePence + workspacePricePence) / 100).toLocaleString('en-GB') %> for both. Which workers you get, and what each one does, is agreed in a recorded planning conversation, the same way the website is, so you know exactly what the <%= '£' + (workspacePricePence / 100).toLocaleString('en-GB') %> buys before any work starts.</p>
            <p data-office-link>You can look round an example in the <a class="tw-link" href="/taxi-demo/staff-portal">Tidewell Cars staff office</a>, where the workers run on a made up firm.</p>
        </div>
        </div>
    </main>

    <%- include('partials/site-footer', { canEdit: false, pageContact, content }) %>
    <script nonce="<%= nonce %>">
        <%- include('partials/site-chrome-script') %>
    </script>
</body>
</html>
